          }\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\"}\nMySQL :: MySQL 8.4 Reference Manual :: 15.1.2 ALTER DATABASE Statement (https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/en/alter-database.html)\nciteturn101view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/en/alter-database.html\",\"lineno\":588}); Total lines: 840\nL179:       * cite88†Parenthesized Query Expressions L202:         * cite100†Derived Tables L203: \nL204:         * cite101†Lateral Derived Tables L205: \nL206:         * cite102†Subquery Errors L207: \nL208:         * cite103†Optimizing Subqueries L209: \nL210:         * cite104†Restrictions on Subqueries L211: \nL212:       * cite105†TABLE Statement L213: \nL214:       * cite106†UPDATE Statement L215: \nL216:       * cite107†UNION Clause L217: \nL218:       * cite108†VALUES Statement L219: \nL220:       * cite109†WITH (Common Table Expressions) L221: \nL222:     * cite110†Transactional and Locking Statements L223: \nL224:       * cite111†START TRANSACTION, COMMIT, and ROLLBACK Statements L225:       * cite112†Statements That Cannot Be Rolled Back L226: \nL227:       * cite113†Statements That Cause an Implicit Commit L228: \nL229:       * cite114†SAVEPOINT, ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT, and RELEASE SAVEPOINT Statements L230: \nL231:       * cite115†LOCK INSTANCE FOR BACKUP and UNLOCK INSTANCE Statements L232: \nL233:       * cite116†LOCK TABLES and UNLOCK TABLES Statements L234: \nL235:       * cite117†SET TRANSACTION Statement L236: \nL237:       * cite118†XA Transactions L238: \nL239:         * cite119†XA Transaction SQL Statements L240: \nL241:         * cite120†XA Transaction States L242:         * cite121†Restrictions on XA Transactions L243: \nL244:     * cite122†Replication Statements L245: \nL246:       * cite123†SQL Statements for Controlling Source Servers L247: \nL248:         * cite124†PURGE BINARY LOGS Statement