t\tn->newrole = $6;\n\t\t\t\t\t$$ = (Node *) n;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t;\n\n/*****************************************************************************\n *\n *\t\tQUERY:\n *\n *\t\tDROP itemtype [ IF EXISTS ] itemname [, itemname ...]\n *           [ RESTRICT | CASCADE ]\n *\n *****************************************************************************/\n\nDropStmt:\tDROP object_type_any_name IF_P EXISTS any_name_list opt_drop_behavior\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"CURRENT_ROLE\"),\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t parser_errposition(@1)));\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t;\n\nRoleSpec:\tNonReservedWord\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t/*\n\t\t\t\t\t * \"public\" and \"none\" are not keywords, but they must\n\t\t\t\t\t * be treated specially here.\n\t\t\t\t\t */\n\t\t\t\t\tRoleSpec   *n;\n\n\t\t\t\t\tif (strcmp($1, \"public\") == 0)\n\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\tn = (RoleSpec *) makeRoleSpec(ROLESPEC_PUBLIC, @1);\n\t\t\t\t\t\tn->roletype = ROLESPEC_PUBLIC;\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\telse if (strcmp($1, \"none\") == 0)\n\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\tereport(ERROR,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t(errcode(ERRCODE_RESERVED_NAME),\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t errmsg(\"role name \\\"%s\\\" is reserved\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"none\"),\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t parser_errposition(@1)));\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\telse\n\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\tn = makeRoleSpec(ROLESPEC_CSTRING, @1);\n\t\t\t\t\t\tn->rolename = pstrdup($1);\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t$$ = n;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t| CURRENT_ROLE\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t$$ = makeRoleSpec(ROLESPEC_CURRENT_ROLE, @1);\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t| CURRENT_USER\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t$$ = makeRoleSpec(ROLESPEC_CURRENT_USER, @1);\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t| SESSION_USER\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t$$ = makeRoleSpec(ROLESPEC_SESSION_USER, @1);\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t;\n\nrole_list:\tRoleSpec\n\t\t\t\t{ $$ = list_make1($1); }\n\t\t\t| role_list ',' RoleSpec\n\t\t\t\t{ $$ = lappend($1, $3); }\n\t\t;\n\n\n/*****************************************************************************\n *\n * PL/pgSQL extensions\n *\n * You'd think a PL/pgSQL \"expression\" should be just an a_expr, but\n * historically it can include just about anything that can follow SELECT.\n * Therefore the returned struct is a SelectStmt.\n *****************************************************************************/\n\nPLpgSQL_Expr: opt_distinct_clause opt_target_list\n\t\t\tfrom_clause where_clause\n"},"started_at_ms":1790154163423,"completed_at_ms":1790154163423}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T09:02:43.558Z","ordinal":18036,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0cd80-c566-7933-9858-a0c84a6c3dc0","call_id":"call_TgjSiwMIivviXk5AMXaGgeHg","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"PostgreSQL: Documentation: 17: DROP OWNED (https://www.postgresql.org/docs/17/sql-drop-owned.html)\nciteturn104view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/17/sql-drop-owned.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 75\nL0: August 13, 2026: cite0†PostgreSQL 18.6, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, 14.24 and 19 Beta 3 Released! L1: \nL2: cite1†Documentation → cite2†PostgreSQL 17 L3: \nL4: Supported Versions: cite3†Current (cite4†18 ) / cite5†17 / cite6†16 / cite7†15 / cite8†14 L5: \nL6: Development Versions: cite9†19 / cite10†devel L7: \nL8: Unsupported versions: cite11†13 / cite12†12 / cite13†11 / cite14†10 / cite15†9.6 / cite16†9.5 / cite17†9.4 / cite18†9.3 / cite19†9.2 / cite20†9.1 / cite21†9.0 / cite22†8.4 / cite23†8.3 / cite24†8.2 L9: \nL10: [Input]\nL11: \nL12: [Input: Search the documentation for...]\nL13: DROP OWNED\nL14: ---\nL15: cite25†Prev | cite26†Up | SQL Commands  | cite2†Home |  cite27†Next L16: \nL17: * * *\nL18: ## DROP OWNED\nL19: \nL20: DROP OWNED — remove database objects owned by a database role\nL21: \nL22: ## Synopsis\nL23: \nL24:     DROP OWNED BY { `name` | CURRENT_ROLE | CURRENT_USER | SESSION_USER } [, ...] [ CASCADE | RESTRICT ]\nL25: \nL26: \nL27: ## Description\nL28: \nL29: `DROP OWNED` drops all the objects within the current database that are owned by one of the specified roles. Any privileges granted to the given roles on objects in the current database or on shared objects (databases, tablespaces, configuration parameters) will also be revoked.\nL30: ## Parameters\nL31: \nL32: `name`\nL33: \nL34: \nL35: The name of a role whose objects will be dropped, and whose privileges will be revoked.\nL36: \nL37: `CASCADE`\nL38: \nL39: \nL40: Automatically drop objects that depend on the affected objects, and in turn all objects that depend on those objects (see cite28†Section 5.15 ).\nL41: \nL42: `RESTRICT`\nL43: \nL44: \nL45: Refuse to drop the objects owned by a role if any other database objects depend on one of the affected objects. This is the default.\nL46: ## Notes\nL47: \nL48: `DROP OWNED` is often used to prepare for the removal of one or more roles. Because `DROP OWNED` only affects the objects in the current database, it is usually necessary to execute this command in each database that contains objects owned by a role that is to be removed.\nL49: \nL50: Using the `CASCADE` option might make the command recurse to objects owned by other users.\nL51: The cite29†`REASSIGN OWNED` command is an alternative that reassigns the ownership of all the database objects owned by one or more roles. However, `REASSIGN OWNED` does not deal with privileges for other objects.\nL52: \nL53: Databases and tablespaces owned by the role(s) will not be removed.\nL54: \nL55: See cite30†Section 21.4 for more discussion.\nL56: ## Compatibility\nL57: \nL58: The `DROP OWNED` command is a PostgreSQL extension.\nL59: \nL60: ## See Also\nL61: \nL62: cite29†REASSIGN OWNED , cite31†DROP ROLE L63: \nL64: * * *\nL65: \nL66: cite25†Prev | cite26†Up |  cite27†Next L67: DROP OPERATOR FAMILY   | cite2†Home |  DROP POLICY\nL68: ## Submit correction\nL69: \nL70: If you see anything in the documentation that is not correct, does not match your experience with the particular feature or requires further clarification, please use cite32†this form to report a documentation issue.\nL71: \nL72: cite33†Policies | cite34†Code of Conduct | cite35†About PostgreSQL | cite36†Contact L73: \nL74: Copyright © 1996-2026 The PostgreSQL Global Development Group\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPostgreSQL: Documentation: 17: REASSIGN OWNED (https://www.postgresql.org/docs/17/sql-reassign-owned.html)\nciteturn104view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/17/sql-reassign-owned.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 71\nL0: August 13, 2026: cite0†PostgreSQL 18.6, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, 14.24 and 19 Beta 3 Released! L1: \nL2: cite1†Documentation → cite2†PostgreSQL 17 L3: \nL4: Supported Versions: cite3†Current (cite4†18 ) / cite5†17 / cite6†16 / cite7†15 / cite8†14 L5: \nL6: Development Versions: cite9†19 / cite10†devel L7: \nL8: Unsupported versions: cite11†13 / cite12†12 / cite13†11 / cite14†10 / cite15†9.6 / cite16†9.5 / cite17†9.4 / cite18†9.3 / cite19†9.2 / cite20†9.1 / cite21†9.0 / cite22†8.4 / cite23†8.3 / cite24†8.2 L9: \nL10: [Input]\nL11: \nL12: [Input: Search the documentation for...]\nL13: REASSIGN OWNED\nL14: ---\nL15: cite25†Prev | cite26†Up | SQL Commands  | cite2†Home |  cite27†Next L16: \nL17: * * *\nL18: ## REASSIGN OWNED\nL19: \nL20: REASSIGN OWNED — change the ownership of database objects owned by a database role\nL21: \nL22: ## Synopsis\nL23: \nL24:     REASSIGN OWNED BY { `old_role` | CURRENT_ROLE | CURRENT_USER | SESSION_USER } [, ...]\nL25:                    TO { `new_role` | CURRENT_ROLE | CURRENT_USER | SESSION_USER }\nL26: \nL27: \nL28: ## Description\nL29: \nL30: `REASSIGN OWNED` instructs the system to change the ownership of database objects owned by any of the `old_roles` to `new_role`.\nL31: ## Parameters\nL32: \nL33: `old_role`\nL34: \nL35: \nL36: The name of a role. The ownership of all the objects within the current database, and of all shared objects (databases, tablespaces), owned by this role will be reassigned to `new_role`.\nL37: \nL38: `new_role`\nL39: \nL40: \nL41: The name of the role that will be made the new owner of the affected objects.\nL42: ## Notes\nL43: \nL44: `REASSIGN OWNED` is often used to prepare for the removal of one or more roles. Because `REASSIGN OWNED` does not affect objects within other databases, it is usually necessary to execute this command in each database that contains objects owned by a role that is to be removed.\nL45: \nL46: `REASSIGN OWNED` requires membership on both the source role(s) and the target role.\nL47: \nL48: The cite28†`DROP OWNED` command is an alternative that simply drops all the database objects owned by one or more roles.\nL49: The `REASSIGN OWNED` command does not affect any privileges granted to the `old_roles` on objects that are not owned by them. Likewise, it does not affect default privileges created with `ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES`. Use `DROP OWNED` to revoke such privileges.\nL50: \nL51: See cite29†Section 21.4 for more discussion.\nL52: ## Compatibility\nL53: \nL54: The `REASSIGN OWNED` command is a PostgreSQL extension.\nL55: \nL56: ## See Also\nL57: \nL58: cite28†DROP OWNED , cite30†DROP ROLE , cite31†ALTER DATABASE L59: \nL60: * * *\nL61: \nL62: cite25†Prev | cite26†Up |  cite27†Next L63: PREPARE TRANSACTION   | cite2†Home |  REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW\nL64: ## Submit correction\nL65: \nL66: If you see anything in the documentation that is not correct, does not match your experience with the particular feature or requires further clarification, please use cite32†this form to report a documentation issue.\nL67: \nL68: cite33†Policies | cite34†Code of Conduct | cite35†About PostgreSQL | cite36†Contact L69: \nL70: Copyright © 1996-2026 The PostgreSQL Global Development Group\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"e8c710\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003959,\"exit_code\":1,\"original_token_count\":635,\"output\":\" *\\t\\tQUERY:\\n *\\n *\\t\\tDROP OWNED BY username [, username ...] [ RESTRICT | CASCADE ]\\n *\\t\\tREASSIGN OWNED BY username [, username ...] TO username\\n *\\n *****************************************************************************/\\nDropOwnedStmt:\\n\\t\\t\\tDROP OWNED BY role_list opt_drop_behavior\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t{\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tDropOwnedStmt *n = makeNode(DropOwnedStmt);\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tn->roles = $4;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tn->behavior = $5;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t$$ = (Node *) n;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t;\\n\\nReassignOwnedStmt:\\n\\t\\t\\tREASSIGN OWNED BY role_list TO RoleSpec\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t{\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tReassignOwnedStmt *n = makeNode(ReassignOwnedStmt);\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tn->roles = $4;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tn->newrole = $6;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t$$ = (Node *) n;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t;\\n\\n/*****************************************************************************\\n *\\n *\\t\\tQUERY:\\n *\\n *\\t\\tDROP itemtype [ IF EXISTS ] itemname [, itemname ...]\\n *           [ RESTRICT | CASCADE ]\\n *\\n *****************************************************************************/\\n\\nDropStmt:\\tDROP object_type_any_name IF_P EXISTS any_name_list opt_drop_behavior\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\\"CURRENT_ROLE\\\"),\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t parser_errposition(@1)));\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tbreak;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t;\\n\\nRoleSpec:\\tNonReservedWord\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t{\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t/*\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t * \\\"public\\\" and \\\"none\\\" are not keywords, but they must\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t * be treated specially here.\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t */\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tRoleSpec   *n;\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif (strcmp($1, \\\"public\\\") == 0)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t{\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tn = (RoleSpec *) makeRoleSpec(ROLESPEC_PUBLIC, @1);\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tn->roletype = ROLESPEC_PUBLIC;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\telse if (strcmp($1, \\\"none\\\") == 0)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t{\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tereport(ERROR,\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t(errcode(ERRCODE_RESERVED_NAME),\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t errmsg(\\\"role name \\\\\\\"%s\\\\\\\" is reserved\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\\"none\\\"),\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t parser_errposition(@1)));\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\telse\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t{\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tn = makeRoleSpec(ROLESPEC_CSTRING, @1);\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tn->rolename = pstrdup($1);\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t$$ = n;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t| CURRENT_ROLE\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t{\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t$$ = makeRoleSpec(ROLESPEC_CURRENT_ROLE, @1);\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t| CURRENT_USER\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t{\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t$$ = makeRoleSpec(ROLESPEC_CURRENT_USER, @1);\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t| SESSION_USER\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t{\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t$$ = makeRoleSpec(ROLESPEC_SESSION_USER, @1);\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t;\\n\\nrole_list:\\tRoleSpec\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t{ $$ = list_make1($1); }\\n\\t\\t\\t| role_list ',' RoleSpec\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t{ $$ = lappend($1, $3); }\\n\\t\\t;\\n\\n\\n/*****************************************************************************\\n *\\n * PL/pgSQL extensions\\n *\\n * You'd think a PL/pgSQL \\\"expression\\\" should be just an a_expr, but\\n * historically it can include just about anything that can follow SELECT.\\n * Therefore the returned struct is a SelectStmt.\\n *****************************************************************************/\\n\\nPLpgSQL_Expr: opt_distinct_clause opt_target_list\\n\\t\\t\\tfrom_clause where_clause\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"47e3b5\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002041,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":39,\"output\":\"To https://github.com/k-kinzal/ztd-query-php.git\\n   2f8734d994..e00704a976  fix/sql-semantics-versioned-language -> fix/sql-semantics-versioned-language\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0ccb0-75a7-7862-941a-ed4430a5b3b7","create_time":1790154163.558785}}}
